@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Expert Route Capture
+
+Use this capsule when a planner needs actual selected-expert demand before deciding whether to change weight residency or admission. The native diagnostic reads the post-selection tensor on the pinned llama.cpp graph. Capture requests only matching tensors in fixed single-token decode steps. The uncaptured arm runs the same model and exact greedy steps with the callback absent. The probe evaluates all eight sampled tokens, including the last one, even if a sampled token would ordinarily end a serving request.
+
+Call `plan` with the exact engine revision, then retrieve `probe` and `geometry` as sealed CC materials. Compare the probe digest with the plan. Build it against the pinned `llama` and `ggml` public headers and libraries. Run it twice against the same model and prompt, passing `off` and `on`, and retain stdout and stderr. Use the sealed geometry reader with the GGUF Python module from the same engine checkout. It verifies the packed gate, up and down slices and hashes the GGUF.
+
+Call `adapt` with the two stdout streams, geometry and a request ID. It requires matching greedy IDs, complete layer coverage, unique in-range expert IDs and the declared selection width. Feed its `cache_lab_input` directly to `engine.expert_cache_lab.validate`. Replay can use the same events under a named byte budget. Packed tensor bytes count logical expert payload only. Capture brings backend synchronization, and the event stream records neither physical storage reads nor whether a weight was resident.
+
+This first binding requires the Granite MoE tensor layout and ordered, fixed-step, single-request decode. Verify the exact target architecture, tensor layouts and hooks before extending it to DeepSeek or prefill.
